  <h3>Key Observations</h3>
  <ul class="findings">
    <li><strong>Structural expansion in 2021:</strong> Total questions jumped from 25 (2019) to 33 (2021), a +32.0% increase. This is the single largest year-over-year change and coincides with post-pandemic exam restructuring.</li>
    <li><strong>Stable period (2015–2019):</strong> Total questions held steady at 25–27, suggesting a consistent exam blueprint during this period.</li>
    <li><strong>New plateau (2021–2025):</strong> From 2021 onward, the total settled at 33 questions, indicating a new standardized format.</li>
    <li><strong>2020 gap:</strong> The absence of 2020 data makes it impossible to determine the exact transition point, but the pre/post pandemic shift is unambiguous.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<!-- Section 3: Question Type Composition -->
<div class="section">
  <h2>3. Question Type Composition &amp; Trends</h2>
  <p>Beyond raw volume, the <em>composition</em> of question types reveals how the exam's character has shifted. The stacked area chart below shows the proportional share of each type across years.</p>

  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <img src="data:image/png;base64,{chart3_b64}" alt="Question Type Composition Over Time">
  </div>

  <div class="chart-wrap">
