n Phase 2 format. Educators should design mock exams around the current 33-question structure.", "   </div>", "   <ul>", "-    <li>Allocate more preparation time to <strong>Short question breadth</strong> — the expanded section covers a wider range of sub-topics.</li>", "+    <li>The <strong>MCQ and Long sections are fully predictable</strong> — 15 and 3 questions respectively, unchanged since 2015.</li>", "+    <li><strong>Short questions are the only variable section</strong> — they have ranged from 9 to 18 across the decade. Prepare for the current 15-question standard but be aware this could shift.</li>", "     <li>Note the emergence of <strong>newer topics</strong> post-2021: structures, pointers, arrays, bitwise operators, ER diagrams, binary search, Fibonacci series, and ACID properties. While not yet dominant, these signal a modernization trend.</li>", "-    <li>The <strong>Long question pattern</strong> (3 questions covering C programming, database theory, and functions/structures) has remained remarkably consistent — this is the most predictable section.</li>", "   </ul>", " ", "   <h3>5.4 Curriculum Alignment Recommendations</h3>"]}, {"oldStart": 689, "oldLines": 6, "newStart": 737, "newLines": 7, "lines": ["     <li><strong>Integrate programming practice into every unit</strong> — program-writing questions appear in both Short and Long sections and span loops, functions, arrays, and file handling.</li>", "     <li><strong>Ensure MS Access coverage</strong> — despite being a relatively narrow tool, it receives disproportionate exam attention due to its role in the BIEK syllabus.</li>", "     <li><strong>Introduce advanced C concepts earlier</strong> — the post-2021 trend toward pointers, structures, and file handling suggests these will become more prominent, not less.</li>", "+    <li><strong>Teach SQL terminology and DDL/DML/DCL/TCL acronyms</strong> — these appear consistently in both MCQs and Short questions.</li>", "   </ul>", " </div>", " "]}, {"old