    <li><strong>Long questions are highly predictable.</strong> They consistently follow a three-question pattern covering: (1) control structures/loops with programs, (2) functions/data types/I-O, and (3) database models/DBMS concepts.</li>
    <li><strong>The exam moved from MCQ-heavy toward balanced.</strong> MCQs went from 55.6% of the exam (Phase 1) to 45.5% (Phase 3), while Short questions rose from 33.3% to 45.5%.</li>
